This directory exists to be empty, and it is the API project's static output.

With no output directory configured, Vercel publishes the project root, which
served the backend's own source over HTTP — /backend/app.py, /backend/config.py
and /requirements.txt were all reachable, and only `.vercelignore` stood between
a stray secret file and the public internet.

Pointing `outputDirectory` at this empty directory leaves the deployment with a
single route table: the catch-all rewrite to api/index.py. Do not put assets here
expecting them to be served — the Flask application owns every path.

See sg/vercel.json and sg/README.md.
